Aspects of the disclosure may take physical form in certain parts and steps, embodiments of which will be described in detail in the following description and illustrated in the accompanying drawings that form a part hereof, wherein:
FIG. 1A and FIG. 1B depict an illustrative operating environment in accordance with various aspects of the disclosure;
FIG. 2 depicts an illustrative vehicle in communication with one or more computer systems assisting in the promotion of good driving behavior in accordance with various aspects of the disclosure;
FIG. 3A, FIG. 3B, and FIG. 3C depict illustrative steps of methods of promoting good driving behavior in accordance with various aspects of the disclosure; and
FIG. 4A and FIG. 4B illustrate examples of possible good driving point assignments with respect to particular characteristics in accordance with various aspects of the disclosure; and
FIG. 5 is a chart of some illustrative categories and their illustrative characteristics in accordance with various aspects of the disclosure.

claims:
1. A vehicle telematics unit configured for customization by a user-defined good driving (GD) wish list and for installation in a user's vehicle, the vehicle telematics unit comprising:
a processing unit comprising a processor;
a memory unit storing the GD wish list, wherein the GD wish list comprises: (i) at least one user-selected com-bination of one or more characteristics of driving behavior, (ii) user-provided values, which are indica-tive of good driving behavior that the user wishes to follow, corresponding to the one or more characteristics of driving behavior, and (iii) an amount of good driving (GD) points corresponding to the at least one user-selected combination; and
the memory unit further storing computer-executable instructions, which when executed by the processing unit, cause the vehicle telematics unit to:
monitor the user's driving behavior using at least one sensor unit associated with the vehicle telematics unit,
detect, by the processing unit, that the monitored driv-ing behavior meets the requirements corresponding to the user-provided values for the characteristics of a first combination of the at least one user-selected combination in the GD wish list;
credit the user's account with the amount of GD points corresponding to the first user-selected combination; and
generate, by the processing unit based on the amount of credited GD points exceeding a predetermined threshold, a positive message configured for percep-tion in the user's vehicle, to promote good driving behavior;
wherein for the same user performing the same driving behavior, a first vehicle telematics unit customized with a GD wish list with more challenging require-ments accumulates more GD points than a second vehicle telematics unit customized with a GD wish list with less challenging requirements.
